Expected elements: present

Every must-show item is on the page and no must-not-show item is: the affirmative green provenance banner sits first with slug, endpoint, moment and replay window; the identity bar carries the truncated hash, `block 63675`, an exit that lands on `aztec-testnet`, eight stepping buttons, `128 / 345` and the phase rail; all three source-less panes explain themselves in their own words; `Supply sources` is present; `effectsMismatched: 0` is legible in the transaction pane. No invented source, no fixture content, no failure banner, no page scrollbar. The previously reported dangling `" / "` and the uppercase NOIR tag are both absent.

In my lens the page is legible but its colour system is inherited rather than designed. Every neutral is mathematically achromatic (#101010/#242424/#484848/#565656/#C8C8C8/#DDDDDD/#ECECEB) while every accent is an unmodified stock value from four unrelated hue families — indigo-600 links, blue-600/100/800 phase rail, cyan-800 progress fill, green-600/100/800 chips — with no shared cast tying the light theme to the CodeTracer dark surface. Text contrast passes everywhere (lowest is the inactive EVENT LOG tab at 5.40:1); the failures are all systemic: no elevation model, one green chip carrying three different meanings, emphasis ink allocated against importance, and two button treatments for one primitive.

Highest-priority fixes: give the shell real surface levels so the provenance banner, identity bar and pane bodies are not all #FFFFFF, and collapse the loading indicator onto one accent hue.

Rating: 6/10

